    "mission_1.compare.arc": "Same results as before -> the odometry results are slightly less than predicted. Together with Trial 1 and Trial 2 is shows a consistent pattern that the robot travels about 10% less than predicted ",
    "mission_1.compare.straight": "My prediction and ideal model parameters matched, however, the odometry-estimated path is slightly different (predicted: 0.45m, odometry-estimated: 0.403m).\nThis can be due to the fact that the robot actually moved less than it supposed to (due to the environment conditions or mechanical characteristics of the robot itself). Robot also could travel 0.45 m as it supposed to, but our sensor reported that it travelled only 0.403.\nWe need to check if that is consistent and the odometry-estimated path is always approximately 10% less than it supposed to be -> we need to run more tests.\nThen, we need to check if the robot actually travelled 0.45 m and, additionally, we need to take a look at velocity (commanded and measured).",
    "mission_1.compare.turn_then_drive": "My predictions matched the ideal model, but differed slightly from the odometry results.\nSame issue as in the trial 1, the odometry indicates that the robot travelled less than predicted.\nSame reasoning applies, however,  since this is the same robot and setup, we now know that this happens systematically",
    "mission_1.error.arc": "",
    "mission_1.error.straight": "",
    "mission_1.error.turn_then_drive": "",
    "mission_1.hallway_analysis": "I would say the most uncomfortable behavior is in trial 2, because a person nearby can't predict which direction the robot will go next. For example, in trial 3 during the curved motion,  people can see where the robot will go next.\nI would suggest changing v when the robot turns, so it motions will be smoother and more human-like.",
    "mission_1.predictions": {
      "arc": {
        "description": "Robot is turning left by 1.6 rad while moving forward\nTheta = 0.4*4 =1.6 \nR = 0.15/0.4 =0.375  \nTheta * R = predicted path length = 1.6*0.375=0.6",
        "id": "d1af6582d25f480f972c32d76f899968",
        "path_length": 0.6,
        "saved_at": "2026-09-25T21:40:00.030035+00:00",
        "theta": 1.6,
        "x": null,
        "y": null
      },
      "straight": {
        "description": "d = 0.15 m/s * 3 sec = 0.45 m\nNo turning, therefore robot will be moving in a straight line.\nFinal position: (0, 0.45, 0)",
        "id": "8289750fef244c61962564156e547837",
        "path_length": 0.45,
        "saved_at": "2026-09-25T20:57:00.623886+00:00",
        "theta": 0.0,
        "x": 0.45,
        "y": 0.0
      },
      "turn_then_drive": {
        "description": "0.5 rad = 90/pi*pi = 90 -> robot turns left on 90 degrees, pauses, then move forward on 0.3 m\nFinal position: (0, 0.3, 90) or (0, 0.3, 1.57) in radians\n\n",
        "id": "bc5df65608ed42d1bcdbd5c40aedfe3a",
        "path_length": 0.3,
        "saved_at": "2026-09-25T21:25:53.369402+00:00",
